  + /// flag-looking text inside string literals (e.g. `git commit -m "use -C"`)
  + /// is not mistaken for a real flag. The quote characters themselves are also
  + /// replaced, so the returned string contains only unquoted shell text.
  + /// Length is preserved for unquoted regions (tokens keep their boundaries).
  + pub fn strip_quoted_regions(cmd: &str) -> String {
